      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if you feel healthy, loading up on greens all at once is risky because warfarin relies on a *steady* intake of Vitamin K, not just occasional binges. Sudden, massive increases in Vitamin K from a large green juice can cause your blood clotting levels to drop too low, increasing the danger of dangerous clots. It is much safer to add moderate amounts of greens daily and report any changes to your doctor rather than trying to \"boost\" them quickly.",
